vement path, write your reasoning and make ONE small edit anyway\n\n## Exploit Mode (Conservative)\nRecent best was updated within the last 5 evaluated candidates.\n\nPrefer a small, low-risk improvement over a large rewrite:\n- calibration, normalization, regularization, stable training\n- avoid adding new heavy dependencies unless clearly justified\n\n\n## History Summary\nTotal prior candidates: 2\nBest score so far: 20.31925200173379\n\n## Suggested Workflow\n1. Read prior candidates\' `eval_scores.json` to determine which changes improved or degraded `final_score`.\n2. For the most relevant prior candidates, read `change_record.md` to see the exact diffs that caused the score change.\n3. Identify one concrete hypothesis supported by history.\n4. Make ONE minimal code edit that targets your chosen hypothesis.\n5. Ensure the candidate writes `proposer_reasoning.md` summarizing: (a) what changed, (b) expected impact, (c) why this is better than prior attempts.\n\n## Output Format\nWrite your modified file to /inspire/qb-ilm/project/cq-scientific-cooperation-zone/public/ywang/meta-harness-evolver/project/test/project-bda/hoss-evolution-workspaces/Sanchez21_down/run-1/candidates/candidate_3/harness/<FILENAME>\nWrite reasoning to /inspire/qb-ilm/project/cq-scientific-cooperation-zone/public/ywang/meta-harness-evolver/project/test/project-bda/hoss-evolution-workspaces/Sanchez21_down/run-1/candidates/candidate_3/proposer_reasoning.md\n\nStart now. Read the history first, then propose.\n\n## Harness Run Script\nAfter you generate the candidate harness files, a user-provided bash script will be executed before evaluation.\nMake sure your changes are runnable by that script.\n- Script: /inspire/qb-ilm/project/cq-scientific-cooperation-zone/public/ywang/meta-harness-evolver/project/test/project-bda/harness_run_script.sh\n- Candidate dir (argv[1]): /inspire/qb-ilm/project/cq-scientific-cooperation-zone/public/ywang/meta-harness-evolver/project/test/project-bda/hoss-evolutio